// ISP fix: split a fat interface so clients see only what they use
interface Printer { void print(Document d); }
interface Scanner { void scan(Document d); }

class SimplePrinter implements Printer {  // not forced to implement scan()
    public void print(Document d) { /* print only */ }
}

// SRP fix: one class = one reason to change (separate the concerns)
class InvoiceFormatter { String format(Invoice i) { return /* layout */ ""; } }
class InvoiceMailer    { void send(Invoice i) { /* smtp */ } }
```
ISP shapes the interface (what clients depend on); SRP shapes the class (what one class is responsible for).
